WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.976
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:09.262 --> 00:00:10.720
JENNIFER CADENCE:
Hi, I'm Jennifer.

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:13.090
And today I'm joined by
Leslie from Globe Telecom

00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:16.239
to discuss how they leverage
Google Cloud's no-code platform

00:00:16.239 --> 00:00:18.760
AppSheet to empower
citizen developers.

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:20.630
Leslie, thank you so
much for joining us.

00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:21.922
LESLIE ANNE HARO: Hi, Jennifer.

00:00:21.922 --> 00:00:23.500
Thank you for having me here.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:24.730
JENNIFER CADENCE: Absolutely.

00:00:24.730 --> 00:00:26.620
All right, so first
question for you.

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:28.600
Why no-code technology?

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:31.280
LESLIE ANNE HARO: So we
introduced no-code platform

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:33.220
because there are
a lot of good ideas

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:35.490
that never really
get into the pipeline

00:00:35.490 --> 00:00:39.460
due to failed business case,
limited project resources,

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:43.900
or just by mere intimidation
of justifying that initiative.

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:45.850
So we see that the
no-code platform

00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:49.030
can provide an alternative
path for a business process

00:00:49.030 --> 00:00:51.700
automation in
delivering applications

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:54.070
without being subjected
to requirements,

00:00:54.070 --> 00:00:57.850
or the constraints of the
standard development process.

00:00:57.850 --> 00:01:02.770
So the SMEs or the end users
are able to solve their own pain

00:01:02.770 --> 00:01:07.272
points or problems through
the no-code application.

00:01:07.272 --> 00:01:08.730
JENNIFER CADENCE:
That's fantastic.

00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:11.497
So what problems does
AppSheet solve for you?

00:01:11.497 --> 00:01:13.580
LESLIE ANNE HARO: AppSheet
enables the development

00:01:13.580 --> 00:01:15.210
of niche applications.

00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:16.760
So these are
applications that are

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:20.900
used for a specific process
and groups in the organization.

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:23.780
Individually, they may
not provide enough value

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:27.840
to merit building an application
in the traditional way.

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:31.400
But these niche applications
are in the long tail,

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:34.290
and the combined value is
comparable with a value

00:01:34.290 --> 00:01:34.790
delivered.

00:01:34.790 --> 00:01:38.340
They are a big or in
complex applications.

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:41.960
So with AppSheet, we are able
to allow employees to automate

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:45.560
their own process without
the need of a developer

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:47.690
or worrying about
much of the cost.

00:01:47.690 --> 00:01:50.330
Either they find
it time-consuming

00:01:50.330 --> 00:01:53.420
to report on a
service vehicle usage,

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:58.380
or when they're on site just
doing simple data gathering.

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:01.720
So these are issues that our
front liners face, but never

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:03.542
really get resolved before.

00:02:03.542 --> 00:02:05.000
JENNIFER CADENCE:
So front liners--

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:06.740
I'm definitely
borrowing that word.

00:02:06.740 --> 00:02:10.789
But that aside, it sounds like
working with this platform

00:02:10.789 --> 00:02:13.280
has helped address a
number of the problems

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:14.910
within your organization.

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:17.667
But how has this product
changed how you work?

00:02:17.667 --> 00:02:19.250
LESLIE ANNE HARO:
So Jennifer, we just

00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:22.790
introduced AppSheet in our
company around four months ago.

00:02:22.790 --> 00:02:25.230
And the result has
been very impressive.

00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:28.280
So we conducted a
no-code hackathon program

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:30.140
as our adoption strategy.

00:02:30.140 --> 00:02:33.020
So we invited all our
employees to join.

00:02:33.020 --> 00:02:36.350
We conducted workshops, then
we gave them eight weeks

00:02:36.350 --> 00:02:37.880
to complete their application.

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:40.790
And that's on top of
their usual workload.

00:02:40.790 --> 00:02:43.910
Now, we saw a number of
simple issues that we

00:02:43.910 --> 00:02:45.920
didn't know still exist.

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:48.170
And employees with
no coding background

00:02:48.170 --> 00:02:52.100
were able to complete and
build a working solution

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:53.930
with immediate results.

00:02:53.930 --> 00:02:57.050
Now, a lot of employees
are reaching out to us

00:02:57.050 --> 00:02:59.000
to learn more about AppSheet.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:02.600
So as an example, currently
we are on budgeting season.

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:05.090
And the finance
guys reach out to us

00:03:05.090 --> 00:03:08.360
to build an application
using AppSheet.

00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:11.600
So they were able to streamline
the budgeting process

00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:14.030
by just using this platform.

00:03:14.030 --> 00:03:18.410
And now, when we introduce
a new process, or looking

00:03:18.410 --> 00:03:21.170
into improving our
existing process,

00:03:21.170 --> 00:03:23.480
it is becoming a norm
to consider AppSheet

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:25.370
for process automation.

00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:27.050
JENNIFER CADENCE:
That's amazing.

00:03:27.050 --> 00:03:30.750
So what actions have you taken
to help your organization adopt

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:31.558
no-code technology?

00:03:31.558 --> 00:03:33.350
LESLIE ANNE HARO: All
right, so the success

00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:36.740
of the no-code hackathon
made a very good impact

00:03:36.740 --> 00:03:41.450
in showcasing our employees, the
winners, and the applications

00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:43.400
they built using AppSheet.

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:47.840
We believe we were able to get
those early adopters to get

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:51.500
their insights and
support for our program.

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:55.820
From there, we also started our
own Globe AppSheet community

00:03:55.820 --> 00:03:58.130
to keep that momentum
going after the buzz

00:03:58.130 --> 00:03:59.630
from the hackathon.

00:03:59.630 --> 00:04:02.210
And to increase
more traction, we

00:04:02.210 --> 00:04:06.200
included AppSheet as a course
in our Globe University.

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:10.250
Our Globe University leads
the learning and development

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:12.870
across all our Globe
business units.

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:16.100
So we also include some
prerequisite courses

00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:20.000
to understand the process
improvement and basic user

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:21.140
experience.

00:04:21.140 --> 00:04:23.480
Our employees should
be able to identify

00:04:23.480 --> 00:04:26.690
the overall benefits of
the solution or application

00:04:26.690 --> 00:04:27.925
that they plan to build.

00:04:27.925 --> 00:04:28.800
JENNIFER CADENCE: OK.

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:30.890
One last question
for you, Leslie.

00:04:30.890 --> 00:04:32.930
Since it sounds like
you're ahead of the curve

00:04:32.930 --> 00:04:34.820
when it comes to
no-code technology.

00:04:34.820 --> 00:04:36.470
Why should others
consider adopting

00:04:36.470 --> 00:04:37.853
that same type of technology?

00:04:37.853 --> 00:04:39.020
LESLIE ANNE HARO: All right.

00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:42.770
So the no-code platform is not
a replacement of our software

00:04:42.770 --> 00:04:44.120
development team.

00:04:44.120 --> 00:04:45.770
We still need to
continue to create

00:04:45.770 --> 00:04:49.700
big and complex applications
to serve our customers.

00:04:49.700 --> 00:04:53.910
And we still definitely need
our IT developer for these.

00:04:53.910 --> 00:04:57.680
But there are applications in
the long tail that are often

00:04:57.680 --> 00:05:00.230
ignored or a deprioritized.

00:05:00.230 --> 00:05:02.480
So we believe that
the no-code platform

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:04.580
is the solution for those.

00:05:04.580 --> 00:05:07.850
Combined with IT
governance, no-code platform

00:05:07.850 --> 00:05:10.820
will help speed your
digital transformation

00:05:10.820 --> 00:05:14.840
by enabling your employees
to become citizen developers.

00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:16.700
Your company can
solve pain points

00:05:16.700 --> 00:05:20.270
in your process that are never
elevated to the top management.

00:05:20.270 --> 00:05:22.580
Not just that, the
employees will also

00:05:22.580 --> 00:05:25.820
be motivated as we
empower them to create

00:05:25.820 --> 00:05:27.428
their own applications.

00:05:27.428 --> 00:05:28.970
JENNIFER CADENCE:
Well, Leslie, thank

00:05:28.970 --> 00:05:32.410
you so much for taking the time
to join us and tell your story.

00:05:32.410 --> 00:05:34.910
And for those interested
in learning more about how

00:05:34.910 --> 00:05:37.850
Google Cloud's no-code
technology AppSheet can help

00:05:37.850 --> 00:05:40.590
empower citizen developers
like you, check out the details

00:05:40.590 --> 00:05:41.090
below.

00:05:41.090 --> 00:05:44.740
[MUSIC PLAYING]

